## Design Tokens

### Colors

| Name | Hex | HSL | Use |
|------|-----|-----|-----|
| Primary | #3B82F6 | hsl(212 95% 58%) | Main actions, focus states |
| Primary Foreground | #F8FAFC | hsl(210 40% 98%) | Text on primary |
| Secondary | #F1F5F9 | hsl(210 40% 96%) | Secondary actions, backgrounds |
| Destructive | #E85D75 | hsl(0 84% 60%) | Errors, delete actions |
| Border | #E5E7EB | hsl(214 31.8% 91.4%) | Dividers, input borders |
| Background | #FFFFFF | hsl(0 0% 100%) | Page background |
| Foreground | #0F172A | hsl(212 12% 3.9%) | Body text |
| Muted | #F1F5F9 | hsl(210 40% 96%) | Disabled states, secondary text |

**Usage Rules**:
- Primary for CTAs (buttons, links)
- Secondary for optional actions
- Destructive only for delete/error
- Never use more than 5 colors in single view

### Typography

| Level | Size | Weight | Use |
|-------|------|--------|-----|
| H1 | 2xl (32px) | bold (700) | Page titles |
| H2 | xl (20px) | semibold (600) | Section headings |
| H3 | lg (18px) | semibold (600) | Subsection headings |
| Body | base (16px) | normal (400) | Body text, paragraphs |
| Body Small | sm (14px) | normal (400) | Secondary text, help text |
| Caption | xs (12px) | normal (400) | Labels, metadata |

**Line Height**: 1.5x (150%) for body text, 1.2x (120%) for headings

**Font Stack**: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'Roboto', sans-serif`

### Spacing (8px Grid)

| Scale | Pixels | Use |
|-------|--------|-----|
| xs | 4px | None (don't use) |
| sm | 8px | Tight spacing (rarely) |
| md | 16px | Default spacing |
| lg | 24px | Large spacing |
| xl | 32px | Extra large spacing |
| 2xl | 48px | Page-level spacing |

**Rule**: All spacing must be multiples of 8px. No arbitrary gaps.

### Border Radius

| Name | Size | Use |
|------|------|-----|
| sm | 4px | Small elements |
| md | 6px | Buttons, inputs |
| lg | 8px | Cards, containers |

**Rule**: Match radius to component size; larger components use larger radius

### Shadows

| Intensity | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| None | Flat components (badges, pills) |
| Light | Cards on light backgrounds |
| Medium | Hover states, lifted cards |
| Heavy | Modals, dropdowns |

**Example**: `.shadow` (light), `.shadow-md` (medium), `.shadow-lg` (heavy)

## Components

### Button

**Variants**:
- Primary: Blue, full opacity. Used for main CTAs.
- Secondary: Gray background, border. Used for optional actions.
- Ghost: No background, blue text. Used for minimal actions.

**States**:
- Default: Full opacity
- Hover: Slight opacity change (90%)
- Disabled: 50% opacity, cursor not-allowed
- Focus: Blue ring (2px), offset 2px
- Active: Darker background (for toggles)

**Sizes**:
- Small: 8px 12px, text-sm
- Medium: 10px 16px, text-base (default)
- Large: 12px 20px, text-lg

**Code Pattern**:
```tsx
<button className="btn-primary">Create</button>
<button className="btn-secondary">Cancel</button>
<button className="btn-ghost">Learn more</button>
```

### Input / Textarea

**States**:
- Default: Border visible, placeholder gray
- Focus: 2px blue ring, no outline
- Disabled: 50% opacity, cursor not-allowed
- Error: Red border (or red text below)

**Sizes**:
- Default: 12px padding, 16px text
- Large: 16px padding, 16px text

**Code Pattern**:
```tsx
<input type="text" className="input" placeholder="Name..." />
<textarea className="input" placeholder="Description..." />
```

### Card

**Structure**:
- White background
- 1px gray border
- 8px border radius
- 24px padding
- Light shadow

**When to use**: Grouping related content, standalone sections

**Code Pattern**:
```tsx
<div className="card">
  <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Title</h3>
  <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Content</p>
</div>
```

### Form

**Field Layout**:
- Label above input
- 8px gap between label and input
- 16px gap between fields
- Error message directly below input, red color

**Code Pattern**:
```tsx
<div className="space-y-4">
  <div>
    <label className="label" htmlFor="name">Project Name</label>
    <input id="name" className="input" type="text" />
  </div>
  <div>
    <label className="label" htmlFor="desc">Description</label>
    <textarea id="desc" className="input" />
  </div>
</div>
```

### States (Loading, Error, Empty)

**Loading State**:
- Show "Loading..." text (or skeleton if complex)
- Disable form inputs
- Show subtle spinner or pulse animation (optional)

**Error State**:
- Red text below the field
- (Optional) Red border on input
- Show error icon or message
- Don't clear input value

**Empty State**:
- Centered message with icon
- Optional action button
- Larger heading + description

**Success State**:
- Green checkmark or icon
- Green "Success" message
- Auto-dismiss after 3 seconds (optional)

## Responsive Behavior

### Breakpoints

| Device | Width | Columns | Font | Changes |
|--------|-------|---------|------|---------|
| Mobile | 375px | 1 | 16px | Stack everything |
| Tablet | 768px | 2-3 | 16px | Two-column grid |
| Desktop | 1024px+ | 3-4 | 16px | Full grid, wider gaps |

### Rules

- **Mobile First**: Design for mobile, add complexity on tablet/desktop
- **Touch Targets**: Minimum 44px × 44px (12px text + padding)
- **Text Width**: Max 65 characters per line for readability
- **Images**: Scale proportionally; use responsive width
- **Modals**: Full screen on mobile, centered on desktop

### Example

```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {items.map(item => <Card key={item.id}>{item}</Card>)}
</div>
```

## Accessibility

### Color Contrast

- Body text: Minimum 4.5:1 ratio (WCAG AA)
- Large text (18px+): Minimum 3:1 ratio
- **Our palette**: All primary/secondary combinations meet AA

### Focus States

- All interactive elements (buttons, inputs, links) must have visible focus
- Focus ring: 2px blue outline, 2px offset
- Never remove focus ring; always visible
- Test with Tab key navigation

### Keyboard Navigation

- All actions available via keyboard
- Tab through logical order (left-to-right, top-to-bottom)
- Enter/Space to activate buttons
- Arrow keys in lists/selects (if applicable)

### Semantic HTML

- Use `<button>` for actions (not `<div onClick>`)
- Use `<label htmlFor="id">` for form fields
- Use heading hierarchy: `<h1>`, `<h2>`, `<h3>` (never skip levels)
- Use `<input type="email">`, `<input type="password">`, etc.

### ARIA Labels

- Add `aria-label` to icon buttons (e.g., "Delete project")
- Add `aria-describedby` to inputs with help text
- Use `role="alert"` for error messages that appear dynamically

## Do's and Don'ts

### ✅ DO

- Use design tokens (don't hardcode colors/sizes)
- Follow the 8px grid
- Keep spacing consistent
- Test on mobile, tablet, desktop
- Use semantic HTML
- Add focus rings to interactive elements
- Keep information density moderate
- Use color meaningfully (primary = action, red = error)
- Test with keyboard navigation

### ❌ DON'T

- Arbitrary sizes or spacing (not multiples of 8px)
- Multiple primary colors in one view
- Remove focus rings
- Use color alone to convey meaning
- Make interactive elements smaller than 44px × 44px
- Nest cards too deeply
- Use images as buttons (always use `<button>`)
- Hardcode hex colors (always use Tailwind classes)
- Forget error states (show validation feedback)
- Forget loading states (disable buttons, show spinner)

## Visual Examples

### Good Visual Hierarchy ✅

```
[Large Blue Button] ← What user should do first

Secondary action    ← Less important

Cancel              ← Least important (gray)
```

### Poor Visual Hierarchy ❌

```
[Secondary action]  ← All same size, confusing
[Delete]
[Main action]
```

## Implementation Checklist

Before marking a UI complete:

- [ ] All text uses correct typography level (H1/H2/Body/Caption)
- [ ] All spacing is 8px multiples
- [ ] All colors use design tokens
- [ ] All interactive elements have focus rings
- [ ] Component matches desktop AND mobile AND tablet
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works (Tab through page)
- [ ] Error states handled and visible
- [ ] Loading states handled (disabled inputs, spinner)
- [ ] Empty states handled (message + optional action)
- [ ] ARIA labels added to icon buttons
- [ ] Semantic HTML used (button, label, input, etc.)
- [ ] No hardcoded colors or sizes
- [ ] Contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 for all text

